## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates a candidate's ability to design deterministic end-to-end tests for complex user flows controlled by remote configuration. It demonstrates understanding of feature flag architecture, test data management, and handling asynchronous state changes. The question also probes awareness of telemetry validation and regression risks when configuration changes mid-session.

## Key Concepts

- **Feature Flags**: Remote configuration controlling feature availability without code deployment.
- **Test Data Seeding**: Creating reproducible user states and regional variants.
- **State Validation**: Verifying correct UI renders based on flag state.
- **Analytics Integration**: Ensuring telemetry events fire accurately per business requirements.
- **Regression Testing**: Confirming mid-session flag changes don't corrupt user state.

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright E2E test for NewUserTour feature flag
describe('NewUserTour Feature Flag', () => {
  let mockFlagService;

  beforeEach(() => {
    mockFlagService = new MockFeatureFlagService();
    mockFlagService.setFlag('NewUserTour', false);
  });

  test('OFF state: user bypasses onboarding', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('/dashboard');
    await expect(page.locator('#onboarding-modal')).not.toBeVisible();
  });

  test('ON state: onboarding completes successfully', async ({ page }) => {
    mockFlagService.setFlag('NewUserTour', true);
    await page.goto('/dashboard');
    await expect(page.locator('.onboarding-step-1')).toBeVisible();
    await page.click('[data-testid="next-step"]');
    await expect(page.locator('.onboarding-step-2')).toBeVisible();
    await page.click('[data-testid="complete-onboarding"]');
    await expect(page.locator('#onboarding-modal')).not.toBeVisible();
  });

  test('mid-session toggle: onboarding aborts when flag turns OFF', async ({ page }) => {
    mockFlagService.setFlag('NewUserTour', true);
    await page.goto('/dashboard');
    await expect(page.locator('.onboarding-step-1')).toBeVisible();
    mockFlagService.setFlag('NewUserTour', false);
    await page.reload();
    await expect(page.locator('#onboarding-modal')).not.toBeVisible();
  });

  test('regional variation: EU users see GDPR consent step', async ({ page }) => {
    seedUser({ region: 'EU' });
    mockFlagService.setFlag('NewUserTour', true);
    await page.goto('/dashboard');
    await expect(page.locator('.gdpr-consent-step')).toBeVisible();
  });

  test('analytics: events fire on step completion', async ({ page }) => {
    mockFlagService.setFlag('NewUserTour', true);
    const analytics = new MockAnalytics();
    await page.goto('/dashboard');
    await page.click('[data-testid="next-step"]');
    expect(analytics.events).toContainEqual(
      expect.objectContaining({ name: 'onboarding_step_completed', step: 1 })
    );
  });
});
```

## Evaluation Criteria

- Correctly mocks the remote flag service
- Covers both ON and OFF paths
- Tests at least one regional variation
- Validates UI state at each step
- Confirms analytics events fire appropriately
- Demonstrates handling of mid-session flag changes

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to design end-to-end tests for complex, privacy-conscious configurations spanning multiple services, data residency requirements, and dynamic rollout strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Feature-flag propagation across 120 microservices via event bus
- Canary vs. percentage-based rollouts and race condition handling
- Per-tenant caches with data residency enforcement
- Cache invalidation and immutable audit logging
- Fault injection: service outages, retry logic, and exponential backoff

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-test skeleton (using your preferred E2E framework)
async function testFlagRollout() {
  const tenants = await seedTenants([
    { id: 'tenant-1', region: 'us-east' },
    { id: 'tenant-2', region: 'eu-west' },
    { id: 'tenant-3', region: 'ap-south' }
  ]);

  // Test canary rollout (5%)
  await flagService.update({ key: 'new-feature', rollout: 5 });
  await waitForPropagation(60000);

  // Verify canary distribution
  for (const tenant of tenants) {
    const flag = await getFlag(tenant.id, 'new-feature');
    expect(flag.enabled).toBe(tenant.region === 'us-east');
    await verifyAuditLog(tenant.id, 'new-feature', 'canary');
  }

  // Test 50% rollout
  await flagService.update({ key: 'new-feature', rollout: 50 });
  await waitForPropagation(60000);

  // Verify all services observe flag
  const serviceFlags = await collectFromAllServices('new-feature');
  expect(serviceFlags.every(f => f.enabled)).toBe(true);

  // Verify cache invalidation
  for (const tenant of tenants) {
    const cacheStatus = await getCacheStatus(tenant.id);
    expect(cacheStatus.invalidated).toBe(true);
  }
}

// Fault injection: service outage
async function testFlagServiceOutage() {
  await simulateServiceOutage('flag-service');
  await flagService.update({ key: 'fallback-test', rollout: 100 });

  // Verify retries and eventual consistency
  await waitForPropagation(120000);
  const flags = await collectFromAllServices('fallback-test');
  expect(flags.every(f => f.enabled)).toBe(true);
}

// Load test: rapid toggles and race conditions
async function testRapidToggles() {
  const toggles = Array(100).fill().map((_, i) => ({
    key: `feature-${i}`,
    rollout: Math.random() * 100
  }));

  await Promise.all(toggles.map(t => flagService.update(t)));
  await waitForPropagation(60000);

  // Verify consistency under load
  for (const toggle of toggles) {
    const flags = await collectFromAllServices(toggle.key);
    const enabledCount = flags.filter(f => f.enabled).length;
    const expectedCount = Math.floor(120 * (toggle.rollout / 100));
    expect(Math.abs(enabledCount - expectedCount)).toBeLessThan(5);
  }
}
```

