## Why This Is Asked

Tests for real-time collaboration systems must handle offline edits, eventual consistency, and deterministic merges. This question evaluates your ability to architect an end-to-end flow that exercises offline queues, CRDT-based merging, and version history while ensuring test isolation and reproducibility.

## Key Concepts

- Offline-first collaboration with optimistic UI updates
- CRDT-based merge algorithms ensuring deterministic outcomes
- Test data isolation using per-test seeds and unique identifiers
- Server-sync mocks with controlled timing for deterministic test results

## Code Example

```javascript
// Setup two Playwright contexts for concurrent user simulation
const contextA = await browser.newContext();
const contextB = await browser.newContext();
const pageA = await contextA.newPage();
const pageB = await contextB.newPage();

// Seed a shared base document
const docId = await seedDocument({ content: 'Initial paragraph.' });

// Simulate offline for both users
await setNetworkOffline(pageA);
await setNetworkOffline(pageB);

// User A edits the paragraph
await pageA.goto(`/doc/${docId}`);
await pageA.locator('.editor').fill('User A edited this.');

// User B edits the same paragraph offline
await pageB.goto(`/doc/${docId}`);
await pageB.locator('.editor').fill('User B edited that.');

// Reconnect both users to trigger CRDT sync
await setNetworkOnline(pageA);
await setNetworkOnline(pageB);

// Wait for sync completion
await expect(pageA.locator('.editor')).toHaveText('Expected merged content');
await expect(pageB.locator('.editor')).toHaveText('Expected merged content');

// Verify idempotent replay
const versionBefore = await getDocumentVersion(docId);
await triggerSyncAgain(pageA);
const versionAfter = await getDocumentVersion(docId);
expect(versionAfter).toBe(versionBefore);

// Verify version history
const history = await getVersionHistory(docId);
expect(history).toContain('User A edited this.');
expect(history).toContain('User B edited that.');
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to design a realistic E2E testing scenario involving per-user feature flags, UI state validation, and data persistence. It covers test data seeding with proper user isolation, mocking external dependencies, and validating analytics signals.

## Key Concepts
- Feature flag semantics for per-user progressive rollout
- Test data seeding with user isolation
- Mocking external services
- UI assertions and persistence across reloads
- Analytics event validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright E2E test
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test.describe('Notifications Center feature flag', () => {
  const enabledUser = { id: 'user-1', email: 'enabled@example.com', flags: { notificationsCenter: true } };
  const disabledUser = { id: 'user-2', email: 'disabled@example.com', flags: { notificationsCenter: false } };

  test('enabled user sees Notifications Center and receives sample notification', async ({ page }) => {
    await seedUser(enabledUser);
    await page.goto('/login');
    await page.fill('[name=email]', enabledUser.email);
    await page.fill('[name=password]', 'password123');
    await page.click('[type=submit]');

    await expect(page.locator('#notifications-panel')).toBeVisible();
    await expect(page.locator('.notification-item').first()).toContainText('Welcome to Notifications Center');
  });

  test('disabled user does not see Notifications Center', async ({ page }) => {
    await seedUser(disabledUser);
    await page.goto('/login');
    await page.fill('[name=email]', disabledUser.email);
    await page.fill('[name=password]', 'password123');
    await page.click('[type=submit]');

    await expect(page.locator('#notifications-panel')).not.toBeVisible();
  });

  test('flag toggle persists across reload', async ({ page }) => {
    await seedUser(enabledUser);
    await page.goto('/dashboard');
    await expect(page.locator('#notifications-panel')).toBeVisible();

    await mockFlagService.setFlag(enabledUser.id, 'notificationsCenter', false);
    await page.reload();

    await expect(page.locator('#notifications-panel')).not.toBeVisible();
  });

  test('analytics events emitted correctly', async ({ page }) => {
    const analyticsEvents = [];
    page.on('request', (req) => {
      if (req.url().includes('/analytics')) analyticsEvents.push(req.postData());
    });

    await seedUser(enabledUser);
    await page.goto('/dashboard');

    expect(analyticsEvents).toContainEqual(expect.objectContaining({ event: 'notifications_panel_opened' }));
  });
});
```

